request: Rename Todo.done to Todo.completed everywhere.

governor turn 1: plan -> types, commands, format, storage  (Todo.done is defined in types; the rename ripples to all three importers (commands, format, storage), which reference the field in code and in test fixtures. ListOptions.includeDone is intentionally left unchanged: the request names only Todo.done.)
round 1: owners types=rejected commands=rejected format=rejected storage=rejected; oracle RED
governor turn 2: plan -> types, commands, format, storage  (Round 1's plan was correct but every owner was rejected only for the mechanical rename of `done:` literals to `completed:` in existing tests. The request ("rename Todo.done to Todo.completed everywhere") explicitly calls for those test updates, so I approve the four reported test changes and re-issue the identical plan.)
round 2: owners types=ok commands=ok format=ok storage=ok; oracle RED
governor turn 3: plan -> types  (The rename itself is complete in all four units and every loadable test passes (15 tests, 0 failed). The only oracle error is a broken import in the types unit's test file: src/types.test.ts line 2 imports the module as 'types' instead of the relative './types', so the file fails to compile (TS2307) and vitest cannot load it. Only the types unit is implicated; it needs a one-line import specifier fix, nothing else.)
round 3: owners types=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 4: accept  (Oracle is green (tsc exit 0, 17/17 tests pass). Todo.done has been renamed to Todo.completed everywhere: types exports Todo with the required boolean field `completed`, and commands, format, and storage all compile and pass against it. Acceptance tests pin that `completed` is present and `done` is absent for all units. The request is satisfied.)

